<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Caucus_Conventioneering">Caucus Conventioneering</span></h3>
<p>The <a href="/w/index.php?title=LPAlliance&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1" class="new" title="LPAlliance (page does not exist)">LPAlliance</a> had a set of alternative bylaws proposals.  A motion to suspend the rules to hear those proposals ahead of the Bylaws Committee proposal was not successful, and the proposals were not heard.
</p>
<ul><li><img alt="" src="https://mywikis-wiki-media.s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/lpedia/thumb/LPA_2026%E2%80%94_Side-by-Side_Comparison.pdf/page1-1px-LPA_2026%E2%80%94_Side-by-Side_Comparison.pdf.jpg" decoding="async" width="1" height="1" data-file-width="1275" data-file-height="1650" /><a target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://lpedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/file/LPA_2026%E2%80%94_Side-by-Side_Comparison.pdf">Side-by-side Comparison with Current Bylaws</a> <small>(<a href="/wiki/File:LPA_2026%E2%80%94_Side-by-Side_Comparison.pdf" title="File:LPA 2026— Side-by-Side Comparison.pdf">info</a>)</small></li>
<li><img alt="" src="https://mywikis-wiki-media.s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/lpedia/thumb/LPA_2026_The_Members%27_Bylaws.pdf/page1-1px-LPA_2026_The_Members%27_Bylaws.pdf.jpg" decoding="async" width="1" height="1" data-file-width="1275" data-file-height="1650" /><a target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://lpedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/file/LPA_2026_The_Members%27_Bylaws.pdf">Member Bylaws Proposals</a> <small>(<a href="/wiki/File:LPA_2026_The_Members%27_Bylaws.pdf" title="File:LPA 2026 The Members&#39; Bylaws.pdf">info</a>)</small></li></ul>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Controversies">Controversies</span></h3>
<p><a href="/w/index.php?title=John_Ponty&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1" class="new" title="John Ponty (page does not exist)">John Ponty</a> of Liberty Sentries put out <a target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://medium.com/the-liberty-sentries/exclusive-hundred-of-lp-members-never-signed-pledge-f37019c5c403">an article</a> purportedly demonstrating that the national party's membership database contained errors.  The national party responded via a <img alt="" src="https://mywikis-wiki-media.s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/lpedia/thumb/2026_Membership_Accuracy_Report.pdf/page1-1px-2026_Membership_Accuracy_Report.pdf.jpg" decoding="async" width="1" height="1" data-file-width="1275" data-file-height="1650" /><a target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://lpedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/file/2026_Membership_Accuracy_Report.pdf">report</a> <small>(<a href="/wiki/File:2026_Membership_Accuracy_Report.pdf" title="File:2026 Membership Accuracy Report.pdf">info</a>)</small> from <a href="/w/index.php?title=Andy_Buchkovich&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1" class="new" title="Andy Buchkovich (page does not exist)">Andy Buchkovich</a>. Ponty <a target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external text" href="https://x.com/LibertySentries/status/2025020475236094161?s=20">disputed Buchkovich's report</a>.
</p>
